---
title: Overlay stack
layout: guide
description: One stack decides which open overlay takes Escape and outside clicks, traps focus, makes the page behind a modal inert, and returns focus when a layer closes.
---

## Layers

Modal, ComposedModal, SidePanel, Dialog, Popover, Toggletip, Menu, ContextMenu, the list of a Dropdown, ComboBox or MultiSelect, and every tooltip are layers in one stack while they are open. Layers stack in the order they open. The top layer takes <DocKbd label="Escape" />, and a click lands on the highest layer it hits.

<FileSource src="/framed/OverlayStack/NestedLayers" />

| Do | Why |
| :--- | :--- |
| Open overlays from the control that owns them. | Focus returns to the control that was focused, or was pressed, when the layer opened. |
| Leave Escape to the stack. | A key that an inner widget stops (a ComboBox that closes its list) never reaches the layer around it. |
| Expect two Escapes from a button that shows a tooltip. | A tooltip is a layer, and WCAG 1.4.13 asks for it to be dismissible. A menu opened after the tooltip is above it and takes the key first. |

## Escape

The layer that takes the key is the top one that does not skip it. A tooltip takes it in the capture phase, before the widget under it acts. Every other layer takes it in the bubble phase, after the widgets inside it have had it.

| Layer option | Escape does |
| :--- | :--- |
| `escape: true` (default) | Dismisses the layer and stops the key. |
| `escape: false` | Skips the layer. A Popover without `closeOnEscape` is skipped. |
| `escape: "pass"` | Dismisses the layer and lets the key go on to the next. A nested ContextMenu does this, so one key closes the tree. |
| `escape: "native"` | Leaves the key to the browser. A modal `Dialog` closes itself on Escape and blocks the layers below it. |

## Outside clicks

A click, or the press that began it, lands on the highest layer that holds it. Every layer above that one is dismissed, top down. A click on the page dismisses every layer that takes clicks.

| `outside` | The click |
| :--- | :--- |
| `"dismiss"` (default) | Dismisses the layer and goes on to the layer below. |
| `"block"` | Stops the walk. A modal is `"block"`: its backdrop belongs to the modal. |
| `"ignore"` | Passes over the layer. A tooltip never takes a click. |

A layer opened by a click is not dismissed by that click. A press that begins inside a layer and ends outside, such as a text selection, does not dismiss it.

## Focus, scroll and the page behind

| Part | What the stack does |
| :--- | :--- |
| Tab | `trap: true` loops Tab inside the layer's element while it is the topmost layer that traps. A tooltip or menu above a modal does not lift the trap. |
| Focus return | `restoreFocus()` goes back to the control that was focused when the layer opened. In Safari a click does not focus a button, so the control the click landed on is used. When it is gone, `returnFocusTo` is used, then the layer below. |
| Page behind a modal | Everything outside the top modal and the layers above it is `inert`. Portals, and roots that set their own `inert` (Modal, SidePanel), are left alone. |
| Body scroll | A modal holds the scroll lock. Several modals share it, and the last one to close releases it. |
| Native top layer | A layer with `native: true` is in the browser's top layer (`dialog.showModal()`). The browser makes the page behind inert, so the stack does not. |

## Custom layers

Use `createOverlay` for an overlay that does not build on a component of the library, or the `overlay` action on the element of the layer.

<FileSource src="/framed/OverlayStack/CustomLayer" />

```svelte
<div use:overlay={{ enabled: open, onDismiss: () => (open = false) }}>
  ...
</div>
```

| Option | Use |
| :--- | :--- |
| `element`, `anchors`, `contains` | Where a click is inside the layer. |
| `onDismiss(trigger, event)` | Close the layer. `trigger` is `"escape-key"`, `"outside-click"` or `"tab"`. You flip your own `open`. |
| `modal`, `trap`, `scrollLock` | A modal layer: `inert` page, Tab trap, scroll lock. |
| `capture` | Take Escape before the widgets inside the layer, as a tooltip does. |
| `returnFocus` | When the layer closes with focus inside, move focus back to the control that opened it. |
| `onCovered(covered)` | Follow a modal opened above the layer, to set your own `inert`. |

## Announcements

A live region outside an open modal is hidden from the accessibility tree in some browsers. `getModalHost()` returns the element a live region should be in, and `subscribeModalHost(listener)` tells you when it changes.

```js
import { subscribeModalHost } from "carbon-components-svelte";

// Move the announcer into the open modal, and back out when it closes.
const stop = subscribeModalHost((host) => announcer.moveInto(host ?? document.body));
```

## Server rendering

Nothing in the stack touches `window` or `document` at import or on the server. A layer opens on the client, and the first client render of a modal that is open locks body scroll as before.
